From 9936f5b6d98fff99f95495192a56d7e0dc98597e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:25:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] provisionELF: Skip sections without file contents

provision packed SHT_NOBITS sections (.bss) like any other: it gave
them a flash address after the initialised data and copied whatever
bytes follow in the ELF file. Programming such an image writes junk
past the program, erases sectors the program does not use, and a
large .bss (buffers, heap) can push the image past the end of Flash.

Skip sections of type SHT_NOBITS: they occupy RAM only and are cleared
by the target's startup code. The provisioning format is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/provisionELF.cxx | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/provisionELF.cxx b/src/provisionELF.cxx
index bc14e7d..eb9eb9d 100644
--- a/src/provisionELF.cxx
+++ b/src/provisionELF.cxx
@@ -138,6 +138,13 @@ namespace bmpflash::elf
 			return true;
 		}
 
+		// Sections like .bss occupy memory but have no contents in the file, so there is nothing to program
+		if (sectHeader.type() == enums::sectionHeaderType_t::bss)
+		{
+			console.debug("Section has no contents in the file (SHT_NOBITS), skipping"sv);
+			return true;
+		}
+
 		flashSection_t flashSection{};
 		flashSection.offset = currentOffsetFrom(flashHeader);
 		flashSection.flashAddr = progHeader.physicalAddress() + (sectHeader.address() - progHeader.virtualAddress());
-- 
